# Release trust anchors of production office servers (legatto_env: prod).
# Installed to /etc/legatto/update/allowed_signers by the `updater` role,
# only inside a break-glass window; a release can never change this file.
#
# Format (ssh-keygen(1) ALLOWED SIGNERS), one key per line:
#   release-a@legatto.pl namespaces="legatto-release,legatto-promote,legatto-index,legatto-revoke" sk-ssh-ed25519@openssh.com AAAA...
#   release-b@legatto.pl namespaces="legatto-release,legatto-promote,legatto-index,legatto-revoke" sk-ssh-ed25519@openssh.com AAAA...
#   canary@legatto.pl namespaces="legatto-canary" ssh-ed25519 AAAA...
#
# release-a: the release YubiKey (FIDO2, resident, verify-required). Public
#   half: `ssh-keygen -K` on the signing machine, then the .pub of id_ed25519_sk_rk.
# release-b: offline backup key (U8); added when it is bought.
# canary: printed by the `updater` role on the canary server
#   ("Show the allowed_signers line of this canary server").
#
# The role refuses legatto_env=prod until this file lists at least
# signatures_required release principals, all of type sk-ssh-ed25519.
# Software keys for tests live only in legatto-offices inventories with
# legatto_env: test (legatto_update_allowed_signers_src).
